.abacus/
tags
*.swp
fonts/berkeley-mono/*.ttf
machines/local-profile.nix
# Belt-and-braces: never let a git-crypt-style key file get snapshotted into history
secret-key
# Machine-local Claude Code permission allowlist — churns per-machine, not shared
.claude/settings.local.json

# Secrets: fail closed. git-crypt was decommissioned (its .gitattributes filter was inert),
# so nothing here is transparently encrypted. Only sops-encrypted *.yaml is safe to commit;
# everything else under secrets/ (raw .env, keys, etc.) must stay untracked.
secrets/*
!secrets/*.yaml

# Issue tracker (beads). Nearly all of .beads/ is per-machine working state: the
# sqlite DB and its lock files, the local history backups, and issues.jsonl —
# br's own full export, which br rewrites wholesale on every mutation and which
# carries every closed bead along with the open ones.
#
# The one shared file is open.jsonl, a derived export holding only open and
# in-progress work; scripts/beads-export.sh writes it. Ignore rules select paths,
# not lines, so an open-only view has to be its own file — there is no pattern
# that reaches inside issues.jsonl.
#
# Three lines, in this order, because a negation cannot re-enter a directory that
# was excluded as a directory. `~/.config/git/ignore` on this machine carries a
# `**/.beads/` rule from an old `bd init --stealth`, which would otherwise hide
# open.jsonl however it were spelled here; a repo .gitignore outranks that file, so
# the directory is un-ignored first, its contents excluded second, and the one
# shared export re-included last.
!/.beads/
/.beads/*
!/.beads/open.jsonl
